{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BkujDZcgTzzAY9CGuB59nh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that re-implements Unix utilities in Go from C-source-derived specifications, verifying parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation system.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Human operator writes PRDs and use cases; orchestrator generates Go code; differential testing harness (`pkg/testutils`) verifies output parity. Shared packages: `pkg/sys` (syscall abstraction), `pkg/format` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils` (diff test harness). Each utility lives in `cmd/<name>/`.\n\n**Current implementation** (trusting source_code over stale code_status):\n- **Exists**: `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format` (R1 + R3 only), `cmd/cat`, `cmd/wc`\n- **Missing**: `cmd/sponge`, `cmd/du`, trivial utilities (true/false/yes/basename/dirname), tee, head\n- **Partially complete**: `pkg/format` -- doc.go says \"Implements prd003-format R1, R3\" -- R2 (ANSI color codes) is not implemented\n\n**Current release**: rel00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure) is the earliest incomplete release. Within it, uc002-format is partially done (R1 and R3 exist in source, R2 missing).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nBy P1 (release-driven priority), rel00.0 is the earliest incomplete release:\n- **uc001-magefiles**: excluded from generation scope by DD7 (only cmd/version is a target)\n- **uc002-format**: R1 (columns/padding) and R3 (size formatting) exist in source; **R2 (ANSI color output) is missing** -- ARCHITECTURE.yaml describes this as \"ANSI color codes for file types and permissions\"\n- **uc003-sys**: complete (source exists)\n- **uc004-testutils**: complete (source exists)\n\nThe next task should complete rel00.0-uc002-format by implementing prd003-format R2. This is preferred over cmd/sponge (rel01.2) because: (1) rel00.0 is earlier, (2) the PRD path is known with certainty (`prd003-format.yaml`), (3) the requirement ID is known (R2), and (4) existing code provides clear patterns to follow.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/format ANSI color output per prd003-format R2\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd003-format.yaml (format PRD -- implement all R2 sub-requirements for ANSI color output)\n      - pkg/format/doc.go (existing package docs -- currently says 'Implements prd003-format R1, R3' and must be updated to include R2)\n      - pkg/format/columns.go (R1 implementation -- reference for coding style, exported function naming, and godoc comment conventions)\n      - pkg/format/size.go (R3 implementation -- reference for HumanSizeOpts configuration struct pattern and formatting function signatures)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format/ component description: \"ANSI color codes for file types and permissions\")\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/color.go\n        action: create\n        note: ANSI color output functions for file types and permissions per prd003-format R2\n      - path: pkg/format/doc.go\n        action: modify\n        note: \"Update implements line from 'Implements prd003-format R1, R3' to 'Implements prd003-format R1, R2, R3'\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement all prd003-format R2 sub-requirements as specified in the PRD -- read prd003-format.yaml and implement every R2.x requirement for ANSI color output\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Follow the exported function and configuration struct pattern from size.go (HumanSizeOpts) and columns.go -- if the PRD specifies configurable color behavior, use an options struct matching this convention\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Use raw ANSI escape sequences only -- do not import external color libraries; only Go standard library imports are permitted per ARCHITECTURE.yaml technology choices\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Update the package doc comment in pkg/format/doc.go to include R2 in the implements line (change 'Implements prd003-format R1, R3' to 'Implements prd003-format R1, R2, R3')\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"One feature per file following the existing pattern -- columns.go for R1, size.go for R3, color.go for R2\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Godoc comments on exported functions must reference the prd003-format R2.x requirement they implement, matching the style in columns.go and size.go\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Do NOT write tests in this task -- tests belong in a separate color_test.go task\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/format/color.go compiles with no errors via 'go build ./pkg/format/'\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Every R2.x sub-requirement from prd003-format.yaml is implemented in color.go\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"pkg/format/doc.go implements line updated to 'Implements prd003-format R1, R2, R3'\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"No external dependencies added -- only Go standard library imports in color.go\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Production code in color.go is between 100 and 250 lines\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":58742,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":58742},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d3cce90-0527-4a5a-b09f-48bb95edd315","uuid":"a5639311-e4ed-4a35-8422-f07b475ce036"}
